{:name "judge-intake"
 :purpose "Judge what the kernel's connectors gathered: for each connector event intake has not judged yet (a Claude Code session, a git commit, a Jira issue or transition, a Slack message, a Gmail message), decide whether the vault keeps it as a card, extends a note with it, links it onto a note, or drops it, in the vault's own vocabulary. Each pass that has candidates is one attempt, so the kernel judges the judging."
 :executor :agent
 :procedure "Run by projector itself, not by an agent session, and it never fetches: the owner gathers with bin/kernel sync <connector>. The pass (the server's poll at the vault's poll.every within poll.hours, or pj intake by hand) reads, through projector's saved queries, the newest intake/<channel> event per channel (intake-newest, the cursor) and the connector events newer than it (connector-events-since); with the vault's kernel block off it has nothing to read and says so. It maps each event to a candidate with the vault's evidence (src/intake/run.ts): a session outside every declared repo, one too short to be work, the owner's own message, an item a note already carries or one declined before is skipped with its reason; commits on one branch, messages in one conversation and an issue's transitions fold into one candidate. It starts the attempt when a channel has candidates, and src/intake/classify.ts is the judgment. For each candidate the model names one kind (ask, promise, info, area, progress, change, drop) and, for one worth a note, a title, a body, facets and a target; the code maps kind and evidence onto a decision: keep (a card in inbox/), extend (a card pointing at the note it belongs to), link (the owner's own artefact attached to the note that tracks it, no card) or drop (a decline with the model's reason, recorded and reversible). The model proposes, the vocabulary disposes: every facet name and value is checked against the vault's .projector/facets.yaml and an invented one is removed, a merge target must be one of the candidate's mechanical matches, and a candidate the vault already tracks (evidence.linkedTo) only extends or links onto the note that tracks it, or drops, never becoming a note of its own. A candidate with no verdict after two asks is recorded as declined for that reason; a judge that cannot be reached holds the channel and writes nothing, so the next pass reads the same events. Every connector event the pass looked at is one intake/<channel> event in the attempt, keyed intake:<the connector event's key> (never the connector's own key), at the instant the connector event happened, carrying that event as evidence, the decision and the reason; those events are the next pass's cursor. A keep or extend is also a proposed intent citing its intake event. The attempt ends done with the pass's counts as its result (seen, created, extending, updates, linked, declined, unanswered, skipped, recorded), or failed when the judge could not be reached."
 :output {:intake/<channel> {:title :string :fingerprint :string :verdict :string :kind :string :target :string :reason :string :evidence {:event :map}}
          :attempt/ended {:result {:seen :int :created :int :extending :int :updates :int :linked :int :declined :int :unanswered :int :skipped :int :recorded :int}}}
 :criterion "Every connector event a pass read has one intake event in the attempt, keyed intake:<its key>, with a decision and a reason; no proposed facet value is outside the vault's vocabulary; a candidate the vault already tracks is only extended onto, linked onto or dropped, never filed as a new note; a pass whose judge could not be reached wrote nothing and ended failed."
 :trigger {:manual true :started-by "projector's intake pass: the server's poll at the vault's poll.every, within poll.hours, or pj intake by hand; the kernel's tick never fires it"}
 :budget {:minutes 30}}
